{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793018587,"nonce":"rM/PYpr2X7pNI9Pd5AIWXKUEzYM=","title":"Studio: expose typed component mounting and isolated preview contexts","message":"Status: planned; implementation has not started.\n\nParent: ashui:d2286369fcac837cdeee0b0dd26c05ba2aa86bbd4c967e330ef1471f26a61c68\nProgram epic: ashui:d2286369fcac837cdeee0b0dd26c05ba2aa86bbd4c967e330ef1471f26a61c68\nCross-repository integration: RayDE:c299bb980e54d48d600312f31a178213d13bc56bc2d3967c4bf42ef9816d6671\nPhase: 1\n\nScope\nProvide the reusable mounting contract for a compiled component factory, validated props and children, its rendered Element and LayoutTree/root. Establish Owner and UiContext lifetimes, viewport sizing, theme/stylesheet/font context and runtime-service fixtures. Component construction, render errors and cleanup are attributable to one preview generation; component wrappers are not assumed to add layout nodes.\n\nAcceptance\nA fixture mounts required-prop and nested components, reacts to prop/viewport changes and unmounts deterministically. Multiple previews cannot change the editor's theme, focus, subscriptions or tree ownership. Repeated replacement releases owners, timers and subscriptions.\n\nDepends on\n- RayDE:03d642c635db571275ac33007da36ac479d027a08d48d0f0a08680788c7ac2d0 — Studio: choose preview compiler, runtime and isolation contract\n\nKeep implementation and validation evidence in this tracker. Follow the parent gate decisions; link any additional concrete runtime/backend prerequisite discovered by the feasibility work. No cloud deployment or new backend language is implied by this planning issue.","files":null}]}